   holder (`rad-ox@users.noreply.github.com`).
2. **Open-Source Maintainer Grant (Complimentary Upon Request).** Maintainers
   and owners of public open-source repositories distributed under an
   OSI-approved open-source license may request a complimentary,
   non-transferable **DRIFT Enterprise** license for their open-source
   repositories by contacting `rad-ox@users.noreply.github.com` with the
   repository URL. Complimentary grants are issued at the copyright holder's
   discretion, are restricted to the named public open-source repository (not
   private repositories or internal commercial workloads), prohibit committing
   or publicly mirroring the `drift-pro` / `drift-enterprise` binaries or
   exposing them as downloadable CI artifacts, and are provided "AS IS" without
   commercial SLA obligations. The grant terminates automatically if the
   covered repository becomes proprietary or closed-source.
3. **Open Surface Unchanged.** Even inside a DRIFT Pro or DRIFT Enterprise
   distribution archive, all Open Integration Surface files listed in Part I
   (`bridges/`, `verifier/`, `hooks/`, `schemas/`, `example/`, installers, and
   documentation) remain licensed under the **MIT License** in Part I.
4. **Restrictions & Disclaimer.** The restrictions on reverse-engineering,
   modification, and tier circumvention in Part II, Section 3, and the
   warranty disclaimer in Part II, Section 4, apply equally to the DRIFT Pro
   and DRIFT Enterprise executables.
